card.statement:
Let $h\mapsto \hat h$ be an involutive automorphism of the skew field of quaternions.
The quaternion matrix equation
$
X-A\widehat{X}B=C
$ has a solution if and only if
there exist nonsingular quaternion matrices $S$ and $R$ such that

\begin{equation}
\begin{bmatrix}
A&C\\0&I
\end{bmatrix}R
=
\widehat{S}
\begin{bmatrix}
A&0\\0&I
\end{bmatrix}, \qquad
\begin{bmatrix}
I&0\\0&B
\end{bmatrix}R=
S
\begin{bmatrix}
I&0\\0&B
\end{bmatrix}.
\end{equation}
